Known WorldCore planning details:

- WorldCore is the external control hub for the user's inner world / CyberPulse Inner World.
- The repo is the external skeleton for systems that already exist in the user's head and planning history.
- Existing systems should be organized and mapped, not reinvented.
- Real-life places can act as anchor zones for WorldCore locations.
- The Mystery Man is the main long-running hostile force.
- Mystery Man clones exist and can trigger soft reset/progress reset behavior.
- Bases, zones, cameras, shields, power nodes, transport, threats, events, saves, characters, AI layers, and ownership/servitude systems are all part of the WorldCore structure.
- The Bag is planned as a mobile main control unit.
- Bag Police Mode can scan/capture Mystery Man clones and transfer them to main base prison systems.
- The Black Hole Shield is the highest single shield and can push out unknown, unauthorized, or Mystery Man-tagged entities.
- All major shields combined can form a God-Level Shield.
- The rank/access system is intentional:
  - A1 through A10
  - B1 through B10
  - continuing through Z1 through Z10
  - Level 10 is the highest number inside one letter before the next letter rank.
  - B1 outranks A10.
  - Z10 is the highest normal alphabet rank.
  - God-tier ranks exist above Z10.
  - The user/operator is God-tier inside WorldCore.
  - Higher divine authority layers may exist above normal God-tier in lore.
  - Lower ranks cannot control higher ranks unless special permission is granted by higher command/God-tier authority.
- Do not treat B1 controlling A10 as a bug.

